{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1562880-the-other-five-paths","id":1562880,"title":"The Other Five Paths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-08-08T16:48:37-07:00","id":1562880,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> The Other Five Paths","content":"When I first started this project away back when the Mage Chronicler's Guide came out (literally over a decade ago), I didn't have the research tools I now have, and I eventually stalled out. But with new tools at my disposal, I'm trying this again. This is <i>heavily revised; </i>I have changed a lot.<br /> <br /> This project was inspired by the <b>Mage Chronicler's Guide</b>, specifically the entry about the Watchtower of Brass and Flame. The idea is to introduce not one, but five new Watchtowers with associated Paths, designed to complement each other the way the official five Paths do, while at the same time also complementing the original five Paths; and doing so in a way where each of the new Paths has an interesting flavor of its own. I first published this on the White Wolf Forums when <b>MCG</b> was published, and I've been tweaking it ever since. The current version has been updated to Second Edition standards.<br /> <br /> So without further ado:<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Paths</b></u><br /> As with the regular Paths, each of these new Paths is defined by a central dichotomy.<br /> <br /> <b>Basileios</b>: Authority and Duty<br /> <b>Chthonos</b>: Growth and Decay<br /> <b>Mythos</b>: Memory and Myth<br /> <b>Technos</b>: Theory and Practice<br /> <b>Xenios</b>: Risk and Reward<br /> <br /> To the <b>Basileios</b> on the Path of <i>Sovereignty</i>, the forces in the world are alive with purpose. They summon the <i>Djinn</i>.<br /> <br /> To the <b>Chthonos</b> on the Path of <i>Balance</i>, the cycle of the Seasons is everywhere, as everything is either developing or fading in turn. They summon <i>Serpents</i>.<br /> <br /> To the <b>Mythos</b> on the Path of <i>Enlightenment</i>, the record of the world is an open book, and they can read the stories that surround them. They summon <i>Eidolons</i>.<br /> <br /> To the <b>Technos</b> on the Path of <i>Excellence</i>, the world is full of potential; when they look at a slab of marble, they see the sculpture that they can bring out of it. They summon <i>Archetypes</i>.<br /> <br /> To the <b>Xenios</b> on the Path of <i>Reciprocity</i>, the world is full of Opportunities and Connections. They summon the <i>Weaver-Kind</i>.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The Watchtowers</b></u><br /> <b>Basileios</b>: the Watchtower of Brass and Flame in the Realm of Mount Qaf<br /> <b>Chthonos</b>: the Watchtower of the Wooden Chalice in the Realm of Elysium<br /> \u200b<b>Mythos</b>: the Watchtower of the Tin Flute in the Realm of the Akasha<br /> <b>Technos</b>: the Watchtower of the Amalgam Mallet in the Realm of Utopia<br /> <b>Xenios</b>: the Watchtower of the Jeweled Scale in the Realm of Wagadu<br /> <br /> <u><b>Path Stereotypes</b></u><br /> <b>Basilios: </b>Sorcerers and Evokers<br /> <b>Chthonos</b>: Druids and Mediums<br /> <b>Mythos:</b> Sages and Bards\u200b\u200b<br /> <b>Technos:</b> Artisans and Craftsmen<br /> <b>Xenios:</b> Traders and Advocates<br /> <br /> <u><b>Paths As Game Mechanics</b></u> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 100%\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Path</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Ruling Arcana</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Inferior Arcanum</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Basileios</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Forces and Spirit</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Prime</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Chthonos</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Life and Death</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Time</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Mythos</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Time and Mind</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Space</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Technos</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Matter and Prime</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Fate</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><i>Xenios</i></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Space and Fate</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Life</td> </tr> </table></div> <u><b>Aedes</b></u><br /> <br /> <i>Basileios</i>: Flames (Forces) and Thunders (Spirit)<br /> <i>Chthonos</i>: Graves (Death) and Roots (Life)<br /> \u200b<i>Mythos</i>: Rhythms (Time) and Rhymes (Mind)\u200b<br /> <i>Technos</i>: Forms (Matter) and Functions (Prime)<br /> <i>Xenios</i>: Connections (Space) and Consequences (Fate)<br /> <br /> <u><b>How To Use These Paths</b></u><br /> <br /> Here are four alternate settings to illustrate how these Paths might be used.<br /> <br /> <u><i>Another World</i></u><br /> <br /> In this version of the Chronicles of Darkness, there are only five Paths; but instead of witches, wizards, alchemists, theurges, and shamans, you have artisans, traders, sages, sorcerers, and druids.<br /> <br /> <u><i>The Ten Watchtowers</i></u><br /> <br /> In this setting, all ten Paths coexist, and have always coexisted. There is talk about \u201cthe Paths of the Soul\u201d (Acanthus, Mastigos, Moros, Obrimos, Thyrsus) that supposedly favor the Subtle Arcana, and \u201cthe Paths of the World\u201d (Basileios, Chthonos, Mythos, Technos, Xenios) that supposedly favor the Gross Arcana; but, like the distinction between Subtle and Gross, it's largely a theoretical distinction. Nonetheless, associations are drawn:<br /> <br /> <b>Paths of the Soul</b><br /> <i>Acanthus</i>: the Name<br /> <i>Mastigos</i>: the Spirit<br /> <i>Moros</i>: the Shadow<br /> <i>Obrimos</i>: the Essence<br /> <i>Thyrsus</i>: the Heart<br /> <br /> <b>Paths of the World</b><br /> <i>Technos</i>: Quintessence<br /> <i>Xenios</i>: Water<br /> <i>Mythos</i>: Air<br /> <i>Basileios</i>: Fire<br /> <i>Chrhonos</i>: Earth<br /> <br /> In this setting, the new Paths of the World get the common Elemental Mastery Legacies, and the original Paths of the Soul get a new set of Legacies based on the five parts of the soul.<br /> <br /> <u><b>The World Has Changed</b></u><br /> <br /> In 2009, some sort of cosmic event occurred, and new mages started Awakening in large numbers to a sixth Watchtower, the Watchtower of Brass and Flame. But that was just the beginning: over the next two years, four more Watchtowers \u201ccame online\u201d, one after the other. It has now been over a decade since the New Watchtowers erupted, and their appearances are as much a mystery now as they were then. No one speaks of \u201cPaths of the Soul\u201d or \u201cPaths of the World\u201d; rather, they're simply \u201cthe Old Paths\u201d and \u201cthe New Paths\u201d.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Science and Magic</b></u><br /> <br /> This setting combines these Paths with Gifted Science from **Mage Chronicler's Guide**. That is, the Basileios, Chthonos, Mythos, Technos, and Xenios aren't Mages who Awakened to Watchtowers; they're Gifted Scientists who have Actualized different Utopias:<ul><li>the Basileios are the Path of Physics, seekers of Type V Civilization</li> <li>the Chthonos are the Path of Biology, tenders of the Garden</li> <li>the Mythos are the Path of Society, founders of the Republic</li> <li>the Technos are the Path of Engineering, builders of the Singularity</li> <li>the Xenios are the Path of Utility, advocates of the Market</li> </ul>Thanks to Dave Brookshaw and Malcolm Sheppard for coming up with the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1161338-mage-translation-guide-the-lost-outtakes?p=1161365#post1161365\">Technocratic Utopias</a> while writing the <b>Mage Translation Guide</b>; it's unfortunate you had to cut them for space.<br /> <br /> Thanks also to malonkey1 on the Onyx Path forums for the sigils (see the linked write-ups).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 09-21-2026, 10:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T16:52:55-07:00","id":1562881,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Xenios: The Trader (Revised)</b></div><div align=\"center\"> <i>The Arbiter of Reciprocity</i></div> <i>\u201cTo exist is to be held in relation within Wagadu and governed from the Watchtower of the Woven Cord. Every breath is a debt drawn from the air; every step is a bargain struck with the earth. There is no 'I' that stands alone\u2014there is only the Web of All Things, and the ledger balances us all.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> [hr]<br /> <u>The Metaphysics of Wagadu</u><br /> Magic functions as a cosmic web of relationships directed outward from the Watchtower of the Woven Cord deep within Wagadu. Xenios mages understand that absolute isolation is an illusion; everything derives its identity entirely through its connections to the wider universe. Although modern civilization separated nature from artifice, the Xenios view traditional commerce, legal contracts, and debts as human reflections of a much older cosmic reality known as Reciprocity.<br /> Within this framework, existence itself requires continuous transaction. Every action ripples across the environment, making every living creature, element, and geographical feature an active participant in an intricate, interconnected system of mutual obligation.<br /> [hr]<br /> <u>Xenios Magic</u><br /> The magical discipline of the Xenios synthesizes relational mapping with the enforcement of the First Natural Law, which mandates mutual support, fulfillment of duties, and natural consequences for imbalances.<br /> <b>Gross Arcanum: Space (The Web of Relations)</b><br /> Practitioners approach spatial magic through relational mapping rather than physical geometry. Distance becomes a measure of emotional, conceptual, or ecological ties instead of miles. By recognizing the invisible threads connecting all things within the Web of All Things, a Xenios uses Space to target, reach, and influence subjects across vast stretches, effectively treating the universe as a continuous fabric of mutual resonance.<br /> <b>Subtle Arcanum: Fate (The First Natural Law)</b><br /> Fate serves as the cosmic enforcer of cause, effect, and return, guaranteeing that actions eventually meet their natural balance. Through Fate, a Xenios audits cosmic ledgers, applying appropriate consequences when vows are broken or environments are harmed. Alternatively, mages can exercise grace, treating forgiveness and future potential as valid currencies to clear a ledger before a crisis destroys a life entirely.<br /> <b>Inferior Arcanum: Life</b><br /> Biological forms stubbornly resist the predictable calculations of the cosmic ledger because living tissue thrives on chaotic, cyclical vitality rather than transactional equilibrium. Consequently, organic life remains the hardest asset for a Xenios to quantify. Because life relies on consumption, decay, and regeneration rather than static balances, arbiters often struggle to cleanly map biological processes into the Web of All Things, requiring advanced practitioners to treat physical bodies as bio-economic portfolios.<br /> [hr]<br /> <u>Symbols and Myths</u><br /> Legal documents, ledgers, and the Tarot card XX: Judgment symbolize the absolute accountability inherent in a bargain struck with existence. Cords, threads, and physical scales act as instruments of tension and equity that measure the weight of vows and ecological impact. Meanwhile, currencies, raw stones, and harvested materials represent tangible tokens of debt and value, embodying the self-possessed mastery portrayed by Tarot card I: The Magician.<br /> [hr]<br /> <u>Animism Without Conscious Spirits</u><br /> The Xenios practice an intrinsic form of animism that avoids personified deities or hidden spirits. Because objects and entities are defined entirely by their relationships, a Xenios can express gratitude directly to a mountain, river, or weather pattern. These relationships operate through natural laws rather than deliberate negotiation. Consuming environmental resources without offering proper stewardship or return disrupts the cosmic ledger, inevitably triggering the corrective backlash of Fate.<br /> [hr]<br /> <u>Three Arbiters</u><br /> <b>Kelechi</b> operates as a keeper of the seasonal threshing floor, a nomadic agrarian mediator who travels between rural farming communes and encroaching industrial sprawl. Kelechi evaluates the ecological weight of harvested yields, ensuring that farming communities do not take more from the soil than they return through ritual stewardship. Recently, a major agricultural syndicate bypassed local soil-tributes, sending a violent shock of karmic blight through the local watershed that Kelechi must untangle before the entire valley's harvest rots.<br /> <b>Nia</b> serves as an urban weaver-advocate in the city's densely packed tenements, maintaining the delicate social and material tethers that bind migrant neighborhoods together. Nia uses relational sympathy to redistribute excess community resources and mediate bitter interpersonal disputes without involving formal legal systems. Currently, Nia is tracking a mysterious fraying of community tethers caused by a predatory loan shark whose magical predatory contracts are actively rewriting neighborhood memories, turning lifelong allies into isolated strangers.<br /> <b>Tariq</b> is an environmental auditor and hydrological balancer stationed where an ancient river system meets a sprawling metropolitan reservoir. Tariq tracks the thermal and material debts humanity owes to the water tables, enforcing strict natural consequences on corporations that pollute upstream. Tariq is currently locked in a tense standoff with a cabal of local mages who have dammed a sacred subterranean spring, creating a massive localized debt spike that threatens to trigger a catastrophic infrastructural collapse across the entire district.<br /> [hr]<br /> <u>Xenios Among the Orders</u><br /> <b>Adamantine Arrow:</b> Ecological and territorial stewards who view warfare through the lens of proper return, defensive harmony, and blood-balance, ensuring cabals do not overdraw upon occupied territory to avoid natural attrition and environmental backlash.<br /> <br /> <b>Guardians of the Veil:</b> Keepers of the structural integrity of the Veil. They treat deep secrets not as isolated commodities, but as vital nodes in a communal web where premature reveals tear the social fabric.<br /> <br /> <b>Mysterium:</b> Restorers of the historical and magical web who treat ancient relics and forgotten lore as carrying inherent ecological and cultural debts, practicing repatriation and reconnection over hoarding a financial portfolio.<br /> <br /> <b>Silver Ladder:</b> Embodiments of sacred stewardship and collective obligation who view leadership as the heaviest node in the societal web, actively balancing community needs through reciprocal treaties and proportional responsibility.<br /> <br /> <b>Free Council:</b> Champions of the gift economy and relational liberation who dismantle exploitative monopolies and artificial scarcity to reconnect humanity to the natural flow of the Web of All Things.<br /> <br /> <b>Seers of the Throne (Usurpers):</b> Operating inside the Ministry of Mammon, they weaponize natural reciprocity into an extractive engine of artificial debt, isolating Sleepers and mages to strip away autonomy.<br /> <br /> <u>Building the Arbiter's Mystery</u><br /> Character creation prioritizes Social attributes\u2014specifically <b>Manipulation</b> and <b>Composure</b>\u2014to navigate complex community obligations and maintain absolute emotional balance while bearing the weight of other people's debts. This is supported by Mental attributes like <b>Wits</b> and <b>Empathy</b> as vital diagnostic tools.<br /> For skills, invest heavily in <b>Empathy</b>, <b>Persuasion</b>, and <b>Socialize</b>, supplemented by <b>Investigation</b> and <b>Survival</b> (or <b>Academics</b>). Recommended merits include community-backed advantages such as <b>Contacts</b>, <b>Retainers</b>, <b>Allies</b>, <b>Status</b>, and secure locations like <b>Safe Places</b>.<br /> <br /> <u>Perspectives on the Path</u><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>\u201cThe Scourged treat consciousness like a conquered province and distance as an insult to be ignored. They rip open doors and trespass through minds as if they own every space they cross, utterly blind to the fact that every forced entry tears a vital thread in the web. They fancy themselves free because they refuse to acknowledge boundaries, never realizing that the very threshold they shattered was holding up their own roof.\u201d</i> [br]\u2014 <b>Kelechi, Xenios Agrarian Mediator</b><br /> <br /> <i>\u201cThe Thistle-born live like reckless gamblers in a collapsing storehouse, convinced that every path can be rewritten and every consequence dodged with a clever twist of fate. They trade tomorrow for today, treating the cosmic ledger as a nuisance suggestion. But the Web always remembers its balance, and no matter how many times they slip through the thorns, the debt eventually comes due with interest.\u201d</i> [br]\u2014 <b>Nia, Xenios Urban Weaver-Advocate</b> </div> </div> </div> [hr]<br /> <u>Wagadu: The Loom of Ten Thousand Tethers</u><br /> Wagadu is a vast, ever-shifting expanse of high-altitude grasslands, sun-baked clay plateaus, and sprawling, living nomadic camps that exist in a state of perpetual migration across the edge of the Supernal horizon. It takes the form of an endless, rolling savannah under a sky of amber and violet, where the stars do not move in fixed constellations, but instead trace the glowing trade routes and ancestral tracks worn into the heavens by epochs of exchange.<br /> <u>The Watchtower of the Woven Cord</u><br /> Rising from the center of a vast, shimmering salt-pan as an infinite spire of interlinked, multicolored fibers, the Watchtower of the Woven Cord forms the architectural heart of Xenios awakening. Built from hyper-dense cosmic threads that hum with the kinetic tension of every active relationship, pact, and journey, the Watchtower physically manifests universal sympathy.<br /> <u>Architecture and Environment</u><br /> Cities and settlements in Wagadu are woven from living grasses, tensile hides, and flexible cane frameworks that can be packed down and moved at a moment's notice. If an inhabitant breaks a guest-right or falls into debt, their portable dwelling visibly frays or unravels. Transactions rely on tokens of equivalent memory, crafted talismans, or sworn promises of future hospitality.<br /> <u>The Inhabitants: The Weaver-Kind</u><br /> The denizens of Wagadu are nomadic anthropomorphic beings whose forms resemble figures woven from indigo-dyed linen, supple leather, and sun-bleached bone. They are identified by their <b>Traveling Index</b>\u2014the sum of their active hospitality bonds, honored pacts, and the distance they have walked in service to the community.<br /> <u>Why it Exemplifies the Philosophy</u><br /> Free of tyrannical kings, stationary empires, or static laws, Wagadu operates strictly on the First Natural Law of Reciprocity and Hospitality. Taking shelter at an oasis without offering song, water-tribute, or mutual protection causes the surrounding wells to turn brackish, while acts of radical hospitality send shockwaves of vibrant starlight across the savannah. Wagadu proves visually that to live is to travel in relation, to act is to honor the bargain, and to exist is to remain anchored in the tension of the Web of All Things.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-11-2026, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T16:56:04-07:00","id":1562882,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Basileios: the Sorcerer</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><i>The Sovereign Commander</i></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Magic is a royal decree governed from the <b>Watchtower of Brass and Flame</b> on <b>Mount Qaf</b>, where vigilant <b>Djinn</b> oversee every spellcraft formula and energetic mandate.</i><br /> <br /> To the <b>Empyreans</b>, magic is a command\u2014an intricate, cosmic web of discipline, royal authority, operational duty, and hard mastery rooted in an inescapable reciprocal covenant. They are the mages of <b>Mount Qaf</b>, navigating a Supernal realm built on the metaphysical truth that true authority is inextricably bound to a sacred duty of care, protection, and responsibility toward those governed\u2014transforming raw, vulnerable chaos into secure, flourishing domains that could never survive unaided. Where others view a chaotic backlash or a simple energy anomaly, a Basileios recognizes that a wild phenomenon is merely a symptom of their own failure to properly govern, command, and shoulder the binding weight of stewardship.<br /> <br /> The Basileios exercise <b>Sovereignty</b>, manifesting it not as arbitrary privilege, but as a steady, guiding stewardship anchored in a two-way social and cosmic contract. Under their rule, erratic elements and isolated spirits are brought into a harmonious, productive alignment, gaining access to cosmic stability, defense against predatory anomalies, and a structured prosperity impossible in the wild. Their Watchtower, the Watchtower of the Brass and Flame, manifests on Mount Qaf as a blazing crucible that forges the concentrated willpower required to command elemental forces and spirits alike. Part high-altitude court and part instrument of cosmic law, it stands as the structural stability of an invocation. To a Basileios, to cast a spell is to issue a mandate to the cosmos while carrying the literal debt of its protection\u2014a ruler whose power fractures if they fail to uphold justice or shield their domain.<br /> <br /> The Empyreans divide their calling between the studious mastery of the sorcerer and the kinetic discharge of the evoker. Many Basileios lean into the role of studious sorcerers who master the hidden protocols of energetic currents, analyzing arcane matrices, charting spiritual hierarchies across Mount Qaf, and refining esoteric formulas against entropy. At the same time, the evokers focus on raw manifestation, unleashing roaring flames, concussive force, and supernatural energies with calculated precision. When a working demands immediate intervention, a Basileios evoker steps forward as a protector who steps in front of their cohort, erecting a fortress roof of force and spirit over their allies. Whether analyzing a complex energetic matrix or throwing up a defensive ward, a Basileios treats energy as something to be governed with absolute responsibility, meaning a mismanaged duty or abandoned charge sends shockwaves through their very Supernal anchor. <b>Basileios Magic</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Gross: Forces.</b> Channels the raw, kinetic energy, natural elements, and supernatural phenomena of the cosmos through the lens of systematic command and protective stewardship. A Basileios treats thunder, flame, and supernatural power not as wild, unbridled forces to be negotiated with or brute-forced, but as unruly variables requiring formal protocols and structural discipline to be safely guided to a productive end\u2014harnessing volatile energies to power communities, shield borders, and cultivate environments where life can thrive safely against the pressures of the Fallen world.<br /> <br /> <b>Subtle: Spirit.</b> Navigates the intricate networks and customary protocols of unseen spiritual domains, guided by the sorcerer's duty to maintain cosmic and diplomatic order through established civic frameworks rather than raw intuition. Through Spirit, petitions and formal accords are brokered across Mount Qaf and the Fallen world, fostering respectful cooperation and mutual obligation between spiritual entities as a prudent ruler engages a community of distinct subjects\u2014lifting local spirits and numina out of parasitic desperation by binding them into a reciprocal web of mutual sustenance and shared civic duty.<br /> <br /> Combined, Forces and Spirit synergize to project a balanced stewardship over both the tangible and intangible domains of reality. The Empyrean sorcerer channels physical elements while simultaneously fostering orderly cooperation with the spiritual beings that animate them, enforcing a unified mandate of guidance born of mutual obligation.<br /> <br /> <b>Inferior Arcanum:</b> <b>Prime</b> represents the fundamental essence of magic and pattern-weaving, standing in direct opposition to the sorcerer's sacred trust. A Basileios operates under the immutable truth that their duty is strictly bound by the inviolable laws of magic, recognizing that such laws cease to be laws at all if a ruler could simply rewrite them on a whim. Prime offers the temptation to do precisely that, granting the power to reshape the underlying matrices of reality and undermine the very foundation of cosmic law.<br /> <br /> To overcome this hurdle, Empyreans might consult a master of Prime, like an artisan, who instructs them in incorporating creativity into their duties, finding clever ways to violate the letter of the law while fully respecting its spirit. By fusing Mount Qaf's strict operational mandates with Agartha's flexible ingenuity, the sorcerer learns to weave new possibilities into their governance without breaking the sacred oaths that anchor their power. <b>Symbols and Myths</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Binding circles and pact-sigils</b> supply traditional instruments representing the authoritative restraint of unbridled power and the legalistic enforcement of a Basileios will over recalcitrant elements, echoing the traditional dogmatic authority, spiritual guidance, and hierarchical institution personified by the Tarot card, <b>V: The Hierophant</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Blazing cauldrons and elemental braziers</b> encompass crucibles of brass and flame symbolizing the ritual purification and raw extraction of force from the ether.<br /> <br /> <b>Oaths of subjugation and true names</b> include ancient linguistic mandates and spoken formulas that carry the weight of inescapable law, reflecting the relentless forward drive, unyielding triumph, and absolute command of the Tarot card, <b>VII: The Chariot</b>. <b>Three Empyreans</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Evoker Mara</b> is a fierce field commander of the Adamantine Arrow who brooks no disobedience from her subordinates, wielding crackling plasmic arcs and subduing local storm-spirits with a single, sharp command. Mara is currently facing a severe disciplinary crisis as a rebellious local demigod continues to flout its service oath, threatening to plunge the city's power grid into chaotic anarchy.<br /> <br /> <b>Sorcerer Al-Hassan</b> is a scholarly theoretician stationed within an imposing municipal archive, charting the cosmic hierarchies of Mount Qaf and correcting flawed invocations used by rival cabals. Al-Hassan is racing against time to contain an unauthorized energetic matrix humming beneath the local courthouse before a structural collapse occurs.<br /> <br /> <b>General Vesper</b> is a rigid disciplinarian who rules her regional Awakened enclave with an iron fist, utilizing terrifying displays of concussive force and spiritual suppression to keep order. Vesper's iron grip is being tested by an underground faction preparing a coordinated coup within the enclave. <b>Basileios among the Orders</b><br /> <br /> <br /> Within the <b>Adamantine Arrow</b>, Empyreans are elite vanguard champions and field commanders who project absolute tactical dominance and crush enemy resistance with overwhelming force.<br /> <br /> Among the <b>Guardians of the Veil</b>, they operate as internal disciplinarians and enforcers of magical law who root out unauthorized spellcasting and punish breaches of the Lex Magica.<br /> <br /> For the <b>Mysterium</b>, they serve as high-ranking theoreticians and elemental scholars who decode ancient invocation grids and catalog dangerous spiritual entities.<br /> <br /> Within the <b>Silver Ladder</b>, they fill the ranks of directors, high magistrates, and operational architects who view leadership as an inherent duty of command.<br /> <br /> Among the <b>Free Council</b>, they act as iconoclastic magi who reject traditional hierarchies, instead wielding raw will to forge decentralized, self-governing paradigms.<br /> <br /> Finally, within the <b>Seers of the Throne</b>, acting as the <b>Autocrat</b>, Empyreans weaponize unyielding command to enforce absolute submission, operating as prominent agents within the Panopticon or Paternoster ministries, utilizing surveillance, state authority, and operational mandates to crush dissent. <b>Building the Empyrean's Mystery</b><br /> <br /> <br /> When crafting an Empyrean character, focus primarily on Mental attributes, such as <b>Intelligence</b> for formulas and tactical assessments, and Social attributes, like <b>Presence</b> and <b>Resolve</b>, to project unyielding authority and command obedience from mortals and spirits alike. Invest points in <b>Intimidation</b>, <b>Academics</b> focusing on esoteric theory, and <b>Occult</b> to understand spiritual hierarchies and enforce formal protocols rather than relying on raw instinct, while <b>Athletics</b> or <b>Firearms</b> helps field evokers direct kinetic discharges accurately. Choose advantages that establish command structures or command respect for merits, such as <b>Status</b> in Awakened or mundane society, <b>Sanctum</b> styled as a fortified command post, <b>Ally</b>, and <b>Holistic Awareness</b> or strong willpower pools.<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;An Obrimos wields lightning like a blunt instrument, confusing divine privilege with true authority. Power is a reciprocal contract: if we fail to shelter those beneath our crown, the weight of their suffering shatters our right to rule.&quot; \u2014 General Vesper, Basileios Adept of the Silver Ladder<br /> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">&quot;A Thyrsus treats the spiritual hierarchy of Mount Qaf with dangerous casualness, attempting to nudge sovereign forces along with sheer instinct rather than honoring the binding protocols and mutual duties that keep the realm from collapsing into chaos.&quot; \u2014 Sorcerer Al-Hassan, Basileios Adept of the Silver Ladder</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-11-2026, 06:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T16:59:10-07:00","id":1562883,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Chthonos: the Druid</b><br /> <i>The Ecosystemic Guardian</i></div> <br /> <i>Magic is an earthly cycle governed from the Watchtower of the Wooden Chalice in <b>Elysium</b>, where Serpents tend every seed of growth above and every shadow of the Underworld below.</i><br /> <br /> To the <b>Druids</b>, magic is the living earth\u2014an intricate, cosmic web spanning sunlit fields, deep soil, and the lightless caverns of the Underworld. They are the mages of <b>Elysium</b>, navigating a Supernal realm built on the metaphysical truth that nothing exists in stagnation, because vitality and mortality are two faces of the same stone. Where other mages see a spell, a Chthonos sees a seed planted in a sunlit garden or a burial marker set into the cavern floor, and where others see a curse, a Chthonos recognizes a disturbance in the deep equilibrium of the land.<br /> <br /> The Chthonos seek <b>Balance</b>, understanding that the universe operates on a fundamental principle of reciprocity where every harvest demands the tending of roots and every descent into the underworld demands respect for the dead. Their Watchtower, the Watchtower of the Wooden Chalice, manifests in Elysium as a vessel that bridges the sunlit canopy of growing things with the silent, mineral darkness of subterranean vaults. Part pristine forest sanctuary and part threshold to the kingdom of shades, it anchors the fertility of the surface alongside the final gravity of the grave. To a Chthonos, to preserve something is to nourish its life in the sunlight, while to release it is to commit it to the quiet stewardship of the deep earth.<br /> <br /> The stewards divide their calling between the cultivation of the surface world and the stewardship of the subterranean realm. Many Chthonos lean into the literal wilds and agriculture of Elysium as primal druids who tend sacred groves, nurture crop-yielding fields, and manage the vibrant, surging life-streams that sustain the living. Simultaneously, they descend into the deep underworldly caverns as wardens of death, burial rites, and subterranean boundaries; when the dead restless wander or decay turns to corrupt stagnation in the dark, a Chthonos Warden steps forward to seal the stony vaults, quiet the restless shades, and enforce the absolute peace of the grave. Whether reaping a fruitful harvest under the open sky or communing with the profound quiet of the earth's deepest strata, a Chthonos treats the terrestrial cycle as absolute, meaning a blighted field or a desecrated tomb is a wound in the planetary design.<br /> <br /> <b>Chthonos Magic</b><br /> <br /> <b>Gross: Life.</b> Governs biological forms, healing, agricultural fertility, and the surging vitality of organic ecosystems under the open sky. A Chthonos harnesses Life to tend the living web of gardens, forests, and fields, ensuring that growth remains vigorous, balanced, and deeply anchored in the richness of the soil.<br /> <br /> <b>Subtle: Death.</b> Controls mortality, the deep underworld, decay, ghost-lore, and the silent transition of souls through subterranean caverns and burial stones. Through Death, the Chthonos manages the necessary rot, the recycling of nutrients, and the guardianship of the dead who dwell beneath the surface of the world.<br /> <br /> Together, Life and Death form the dual engine of terrestrial equilibrium. Life sparks the green expansion of the surface world while Death provides the subterranean rest and mineral decay of the underworld, perfectly mirroring the path's core theme of perpetual cyclical balance between earth and grave.<br /> <br /> <b>Inferior Arcanum</b> Time represents the rigid, linear progression of temporal moments which resists the fluid, cyclical rhythms of Elysium, making chronomancy an alien discipline for those attuned to natural seasons.<br /> <br /> To master this hurdle, stewards might consult a master of Time, who reframes chronology through the lens of ancient narrative memory and epochal storytelling. By blending Elysium's seasonal cadence with Akasha's historical archives, the Chthonos learns to view time not as a ticking mechanical clock, but as the enduring rings of an ancient oak or the sedimentary strata recording the grand epochs of the earth.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols and Myths</b> Groves, roots, and tilled fields comprise tangled plant life, crops, and sacred earth symbolizing the fertile vitality and unbridled radiance of the surface world, echoing the radiant life force and unvarnished truth embodied by the Tarot card, <b>XIX: The Sun</b>. Crypts, bedrock, and subterranean caverns act as deep stone vaults that hold the silent domain of the dead and the mysteries of the underworld, mirroring the solitary introspection, profound isolation, and vigilant interior guardianship of the Tarot card, <b>IX: The Hermit</b>. Serpents, bones, and wooden chalices embody shedding, rebirth, mortality, and the necessary balance between harvest and decay.<br /> <br /> <b>Three stewards</b><br /> <br /> Elder Corin is a wild-eyed permaculturist who tends an urban greenhouse sanctuary, using surging life-streams to heal blighted city lots while fiercely protecting local green spaces from industrial development. Corin is currently struggling to contain a series of unnatural, necrotic growths spreading through the local botanical gardens.<br /> <br /> Briar is a grim subterranean warden who oversees the old catacombs beneath the city, sealing restless shades and ensuring that the dead remain undisturbed in their mineral silence. Briar is dealing with a dangerous breach in a deep burial vault where an ancient, unquiet spirit has escaped its confines.<br /> <br /> Talon is a wandering pastoral steward who mediates disputes between rural farming communities and local wildlife spirits, enforcing organic consensus and fair resource sharing. Talon is grappling with an escalating ecological backlash after a sacred grove was desecrated by local poachers.<br /> <br /> <b>Chthonos among the Orders</b><br /> <br /> Within the <b>Adamantine Arrow</b>, stewards serve as frontline bio-sentinels and battlefield medics who channel vital energy to sustain troops while maintaining grim, unyielding defensive lines inspired by the unbreakable rock of the underworld.<br /> <br /> Among the <b>Guardians of the Veil</b>, they act as biological containment specialists and grave-wardens who police the boundaries between the living, the dead, and the subterranean spirit wilds.<br /> <br /> For the <b>Mysterium</b>, they function as natural historians, paleo-occultists, and subterranean ecologists who study the deep evolutionary cycles of the Supernal earth and the lore buried in ancient tombs.<br /> <br /> Within the <b>Silver Ladder</b>, they take on the mantle of tribal chieftains, pastoral stewards, and sustainable community leaders who govern through organic consensus and the careful management of communal land and resources.<br /> <br /> Among the <b>Free Council</b>, they emerge as eco-anarchists, permaculturists, and biotech reformers who integrate modern sustainable agriculture with ancient earth-lore.<br /> <br /> Finally, within the <b>Seers of the Throne</b>, acting as the <b>Harvester</b>, stewards treat living ecosystems and human populations as crops to be cultivated or resources to be culled in the dark, finding their place within the Hegemonic Ministry or localized exploitation cells, reducing vitality and mortality to calculated metrics of state utility.<br /> <br /> <b>Building the Steward's Mystery</b><br /> <br /> When designing a steward character, balance Physical attributes, such as <i>Stamina</i> and <i>Strength</i> for wilderness survival or physical labor, with Mental attributes, like <i>Resolve</i> and <i>Composure</i>, to maintain inner equilibrium against corruption and decay. Focus your skill points on <i>Survival</i>, <i>Medicine</i> for natural remedies and body maintenance, and <i>Crafts</i> or <i>Animal Ken</i>, while adding points to <i>Investigation</i> or <i>Occult</i> for tracking crypts, ghost lore, and ecological anomalies. Choose advantages that establish land stewardship and deep roots for merits, such as <i>Safe Place</i> configured as a grove, greenhouse, or underground catacomb, <i>Animal Affinity</i>, <i>Fleet of Foot</i>, or <i>Famous</i> among local preservationist or underground circles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;A Thyrsus treats the wild like an untamed predator to wrestle with bare-handed for a cheap adrenaline rush, completely ignoring that nature requires careful seasonal pruning and respectful husbandry if it is to survive.&quot; \u2014 Elder Corin, Chthonos Druid of the Free Council<br /> <br /> &quot;A Moros stares so deeply into the terminal finality of the grave that they treat death like an end in itself, forgetting that the purpose of burial is about the patient recycling of nutrients so that new life can eventually break through the soil.&quot; \u2014 Briar, Chthonos Warden of the Mysterium </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-10-2026, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T17:01:07-07:00","id":1562884,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Mythos: the Bard</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><i>The Epic Chronicler</i></div> <i>Magic is an eternal lore governed from the Watchtower of the Tin Flute in <b>Akasha</b>, where whimsical <b>Muses</b> inspire every myth, memory, and cosmic song.</i><br /> <br /> To the <b>Chroniclers</b>, magic is a tale\u2014an intricate, cosmic web of memory, archetype, resonance, and narrative truth. They are the mages of <b>Akasha</b>, navigating a Supernal realm built on the metaphysical truth that nothing exists without a history, because narrative is the foundation of reality. Where other mages see a spell, a Mythos sees a verse spoken, and where others see a curse, a Mythos recognizes an unresolved plotline.<br /> <br /> The Mythos share <b>Lore</b>, understanding that the universe operates on a fundamental principle of narrative where every action, every spell, and every legend demands remembrance or yields obscurity. Their Watchtower, the Watchtower of the Tin Flute, manifests in Akasha as a soaring auditorium that holds the absolute resonance of historical memory, cultural archetypes, and cosmic truths. Part bardic stage and part instrument of high epic, it projects the equity of a tale alongside the truth of a forgotten epoch. To a Mythos, to remember something is to bring it into reality, while to deem it forgotten is to cast it into the void of non-existence.<br /> <br /> The chroniclers divide their calling between the poetic resonance of the bard and the scholarship of the sage. Many Mythos lean into the performance of the bard to focus on oral poetry, musical composition, lyrical expression, and dramatic performance, striving to make the truths they channel deeply evocative while weaving soaring ballads and breathing life into collective myth through voice and instrument. In parallel, the sages focus on the scholarship of history, trading in ancient secrets, conceptual myths, and rare tales while delving into the vast archives that span the Supernal. To a sage, knowledge is fluid and must be continuously calculated against memory and meaning. Whether striking a resonant chord, reciting an epic poem, or unearthing a forgotten myth, a Mythos treats a tale as absolute, meaning a forgotten myth is a rent in the paradigm of truth.<br /> <br /> <b>Mythos Magic</b><br /> <br /> <b>Gross: Time.</b> Governs history, memory, prophecy, and the flow of temporal epochs, viewed through the bardic lens of eternal storytelling. A Mythos uses Time to sequence the verses of history, unearthing forgotten epochs and weaving past events into the living tapestry of the present.<br /> <br /> <b>Subtle: Mind.</b> Controls thoughts, archetypes, cultural resonance, and perception, guided by the sage's mastery of lore. Through Mind, the Mythos shapes how conscious minds internalize narrative patterns, planting enduring motifs and cultural myths that dictate what society remembers and values.<br /> <br /> In practice, Time and Mind synergize to manipulate the very architecture of narrative lore. Time preserves and sequences historical epochs while Mind shapes how conscious minds perceive and internalize those memories, turning legends into living cultural truths.<br /> <br /> <b>Inferior Arcanum</b> Space involves fixed physical distance and absolute geography that resist the fluid, conceptual boundaries of Akasha, making spatial manipulation a persistent challenge for the lore-masters.<br /> <br /> To transcend this limitation, chroniclers might consult a master of Space such as a trader, who teaches them to map geography through the lens of value, commerce, and interpersonal importance. By integrating Akasha's narrative flow with the Emporium's economic tethers, the Mythos learns that distance is less important than meaning; by learning to view Space through the lens of Sympathetic connections, the Mythos leverages their own capacity to make people care about their tales into an ability to manipulate those connections, treating physical space not as a barrier of absolute miles, but as a change of scene or a shift in dramatic perspective where moving across geography is simply walking from one act of a grand play to another.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols and Myths</b> Flutes and instruments represent musical tools that channel the primordial resonance and songs of creation, mirroring the continuous rotation of life's cycles, fate, and performance embodied by the Tarot card, <b>X: The Wheel of Fortune</b>. Auditoriums and archives encompass vast halls of memory and performance spaces symbolizing the eternal preservation of history and myth, resonant with the veiled intuition, sacred keeper of archives, and hidden wisdom of the Tarot card, <b>II: The High Priestess</b>. Scrolls and epics feature written records of legend that anchor narrative truth into reality.<br /> <br /> <b>Three chroniclers</b><br /> <br /> Faelar is an avant-garde performance poet who hacks contemporary pop-culture archetypes in underground clubs, using hypnotic verses to awaken Sleeper minds to forgotten epochs. Faelar is currently battling a dangerous cultural meme that is actively erasing local historical memory in the district.<br /> <br /> Sage Theron is a meticulous archivist and mythographer who spends his days buried in municipal records and ancient scrolls, tracing the lineage of lost spells through oral tradition. Theron is desperately searching for a stolen manuscript detailing the city's founding myth before a rival faction successfully alters the historical record.<br /> <br /> Lyra is a traveling war-poet and morale officer for local cabals, embedding heroic mythos directly into collective memory through inspiring battle-hymns and epic verse. Lyra is struggling with a fading song-shrine whose weakening notes are triggering erratic temporal anomalies in the arts district.<br /> <br /> <b>Mythos among the Orders</b><br /> <br /> Within the <b>Adamantine Arrow</b>, chroniclers act as war-poets, morale officers, and chroniclers of martial deeds who embed heroic mythos directly into the collective memory of the cabal through inspiring battle-hymns and epic verse.<br /> <br /> Among the <b>Guardians of the Veil</b>, they serve as memory-weavers and cover-story architects who spin cultural fabrications, folkloric songs, and theatrical screens to mask the Supernal from the Sleeper world.<br /> <br /> For the <b>Mysterium</b>, they are master librarians, mythographers, and historians of the arcane who safeguard forgotten lore and trace the lineage of ancient spells through oral tradition and lyric verse.<br /> <br /> Within the <b>Silver Ladder</b>, they function as cultural statesmen, propagandists, and myth-makers who shape public narrative and collective identity through powerful public speaking and ceremonial song to cement political legitimacy.<br /> <br /> Among the <b>Free Council</b>, they operate as modern performance artists, spoken-word poets, and musicians who hack contemporary pop-culture archetypes to awaken the masses.<br /> <br /> Finally, within the <b>Seers of the Throne</b>, acting as the <b>Censor</b>, chroniclers rewrite history and manufacture collective consensus to enforce the Lie, operating as formidable operatives within the Ministry of Propaganda or ideological control blocks, chaining human memory and song to the service of the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> <b>Building the Chronicler's Mystery</b><br /> <br /> When building a chronicler character, focus on Social attributes, such as <i>Presence</i> and <i>Manipulation</i> to captivate audiences and inspire belief, backed by Mental attributes like <i>Intelligence</i> for historical research and deep lore recall. Invest heavily in <i>Expression</i> covering performance, poetry, and music, alongside <i>Persuasion</i> and <i>Academics</i> or <i>Investigation</i> to scour historical archives and craft compelling public narratives. Select advantages that enhance cultural influence and memory access for merits, such as <i>Famous</i>, <i>Language</i>, <i>Library</i> representing vast personal archives of myth and lore, or <i>Contacts</i> within media and academic circles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;A Mastigos tears through the mental and spatial fabric of the world like a clumsy brawler, treating the rich, layered mythologies of human consciousness as mere walls to kick down rather than grand epics to be sung.&quot; \u2014 Faelar, Mythos Bard of the Free Council<br /> <br /> &quot;An Acanthus treats the deep archives of destiny like a disposable draft, assuming they can endlessly improvise over established structural canons without understanding the historical weight of the precedents they break.&quot; \u2014 Sage Theron, Mythos Scholar of the Mysterium </div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-10-2026, 08:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T17:04:58-07:00","id":1562886,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>Technos: the Artisan</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><i>The Master Maker</i></div> <br /> <br /> <i>Magic is an engineered marvel and a source of boundless wonder governed from the Watchtower of the Amalgam Mallet in <b>Agartha</b>, where tireless <b>Golems</b> forge every astonishing device, sweeping architecture, intricate mechanism, and sublime sculpture.</i><br /> <br /> To the <b>Makers</b>, magic is a blueprint of utility, beauty, and breathtaking astonishment\u2014an intricate, cosmic web of mechanics, structure, aesthetics, and design. They are the mages of <b>Agartha</b>, navigating a Supernal realm built on the metaphysical truth that nothing exists without form, because functionality, expression, and awe are the three measures of creation. Where other mages see a spell, a Technos sees a precision engine of marvels, a breathtaking painting, a complex mechanical clockwork, or an evocative monument capable of stopping time, and where others see a flaw, a Technos recognizes a failure of imagination or engineering.<br /> <br /> The Technos pursue <b>Wonder</b>, understanding that the universe operates on a fundamental principle of design where every action, every spell, and every crafted work demands absolute devotion to awe-inspiring innovation, imaginative revelation, and the sparking of profound astonishment rather than dry functional utility. Their Watchtower, the Watchtower of the Amalgam Mallet, manifests in Agartha as a titanic grand workshop that houses the absolute perfection of structural integrity, artistic expression, and cosmic blueprints designed to leave mortal and immortal minds alike breathless. Part master studio and part instrument of absolute engineering, it secures the efficiency of a machine alongside the emotional resonance of a masterpiece. To a Technos, to build or shape something is to bring a miracle into absolute realization, while to deem it uninspired or poorly engineered is to cast it into the void of obsolescence.<br /> <br /> The makers treat their craft more like an art than a science, where careful, rigid precision often takes a back seat to fluid, intuitive improvisation. They divide their calling between the visionary scope of the artisan and the hands-on execution of the craftsman, with both archetypes dedicated equally to the pursuit of function, beauty, and astonishment. The artisans encompass visionary engineers and expressive artists who look to grand theoretical designs, sketching impossible architectures, conceptualizing aesthetic frameworks, and weaving the grand blueprints of Agartha into tangible reality. Meanwhile, the craftsmen encompass master mechanics and skilled sculptors who focus on direct, physical realization, turning raw matter into functional machinery or striking statues that balance rigorous structural integrity with profound aesthetic beauty. Whether engineering a complex automated defense grid that defies belief, mixing pigments for a living canvas that shifts with the viewer's emotions, tuning a complex gear train, or chipping away at marble to capture the grace of a Supernal form, a Technos treats their creation as absolute, meaning a flawed design or an uninspired execution is a breach in the foundations of the world.<br /> <br /> <b>Technos Magic</b><br /> <br /> <b>Gross: Matter.</b> Governs physical substances, atomic structures, and material fabrication, viewed through the workshop and studio lens of the artisan and craftsman. A Technos shapes raw elements, stone, metal, or composite materials, altering structural and aesthetic integrity to construct advanced machinery, durable infrastructure, or exquisite sculptures and canvases that meet exact design specifications, forming the practical implementation of their work.<br /> <br /> <b>Subtle: Prime.</b> Controls raw pattern, magical energy, and Supernal resonance, directed by the creator's quest for functional and aesthetic perfection. Through Prime, the Technos establishes the high theoretical framework of the design, weaving arcane patterns into physical matter, forging enchanted artifacts, and breathing numinous grace into a work of fine art and mechanical marvel.<br /> <br /> Together, Matter and Prime achieve ultimate technical and artistic synergy. Prime supplies the theoretical framework and foundational pattern, while Matter delivers the practical implementation, turning cold metal or blank stone into a living, functional marvel or a transcendent aesthetic experience.<br /> <br /> <b>Inferior Arcanum</b> Fate features the fluid, unpredictable nature of probabilities and luck which defies the precise blueprints and structural laws of Agartha, making destiny a frustrating wildcard for mechanical and artistic mages.<br /> <br /> To master this capricious element, visionary makers collaborate with masters of Fate such as advocates, who reframe probability through the lens of legal bindings, contractual risk assessment, and systemic trade adjustments. By combining Agartha's structural rigidity with the Emporium's contractual calculus, the Technos learns to treat luck not as blind chance, but as the complex kinetic feedback loop of an unstable engine that must be housed within robust mechanical dampeners and legally binding structural margins of error.<br /> <br /> <b>Symbols and Myths</b> Forges, studios, and workshops serve as creative spaces symbolizing the shaping of form, structure, and reality, reflecting the ultimate realization, harmonious synthesis, and cosmic completion embodied by the Tarot card, <b>XXI: The World</b>. Mallets, chisels, wrenches, and brushes encompass instruments of precision and expression that transform raw matter into functional marvels and fine art, channeling the sudden physical breakthroughs, structural upheavals, and dynamic engineering prowess of the Tarot card, <b>XVI: The Tower</b>. Blueprints, schematics, and cogs include technical and artistic plans representing the absolute design, aesthetics, and structural integrity of the cosmos.<br /> <br /> <b>Three makers</b><br /> <br /> Master Smith Bram is an eccentric technomancer and avant-garde sculptor who runs an underground forge, turning discarded industrial scrap into living, self-repairing mechanical art installations. Bram is currently dealing with an experimental automaton that has gained unauthorized sapience and fled into the city's transit network.<br /> <br /> Forge-Master Kaelen is a meticulous weaponsmith and structural engineer for the Adamantine Arrow, crafting impeccably balanced armaments and secure sanctum defenses that defy conventional physics. Kaelen is scrambling to recover a stolen batch of rare Supernal alloys before a rogue artificer finishes building an unstable siege engine.<br /> <br /> Aria is a visionary civic architect who weaves aesthetic design with high arcane theory, drafting impossible urban layouts that stabilize local magical nodes. Aria is facing a frustrating wave of unexplained structural failures threatening her latest civic project.<br /> <br /> <b>Technos among the Orders</b><br /> <br /> Within the <b>Adamantine Arrow</b>, makers serve as master armorers, siege-engineers, and tactical hardware developers who construct high-tech implements of war, beautifully balanced weapons, and secure sanctum defenses.<br /> <br /> Among the <b>Guardians of the Veil</b>, they operate as counter-intelligence hardware specialists and aesthetic fabricators who build arcane-tech jammers, secure communication arrays, and forge flawless forgeries or psychological art installations to mask the Supernal.<br /> <br /> For the <b>Mysterium</b>, they function as master artificers, curators, and techno-archaeologists who reverse-engineer ancient Supernal constructs and preserve priceless magical artwork and artifacts.<br /> <br /> Within the <b>Silver Ladder</b>, they act as infrastructural architects, urban planners, and royal court designers who build the physical, civic, and aesthetic frameworks that allow Awakened society to scale with grace and authority.<br /> <br /> Among the <b>Free Council</b>, they form the core of the technomancer and avant-garde artisan factions, spearheading digital magic, cybernetic enhancements, immersive modern art, and the seamless fusion of modern engineering with the expressive arts.<br /> <br /> Finally, within the <b>Seers of the Throne</b>, acting as the <b>Taskmaster</b>, makers construct unyielding automated control grids, mass-surveillance architectures, and soul-crushing propaganda art that reduce humanity to cogs in a machine, dominating the Panopticon and industrial-technological ministries.<br /> <br /> <b>Building the Maker's Mystery</b><br /> <br /> When designing a maker character, emphasize Mental attributes, such as <i>Intelligence</i> for blueprints and physics, and <i>Wits</i> for troubleshooting, alongside manual dexterity handled by Physical attributes like <i>Dexterity</i>. Max out skills in <i>Crafts</i> encompassing mechanics, sculpting, electronics, or fine art, <i>Science</i> for physics and materials, and <i>Computer</i> or <i>Investigation</i> for tech integration and artifact study. Choose advantages that establish a creative base and access to rare materials for merits, such as <i>Workshop</i> styled as a fully equipped studio or forge, <i>Resources</i>, <i>Anonymity</i>, and <i>Artifact</i> creation credentials.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;A Moros treats raw matter like a corpse on a slab, viewing material creation purely through the lens of rot and utility while stripping every ounce of vibrant aesthetic expression and living form out of the work.&quot; \u2014 Master Smith Bram, Technos Craftsman of the Free Council<br /> <br /> &quot;An Obrimos seeks raw ether just as we seek physical form, yet while we channel the sublime blueprint of Agartha into tangible artistry, they merely channel raw voltage through the ether, mistaking unfiltered thunder for true creation.&quot; \u2014 Forge-Master Kaelen, Technos Artisan of the Adamantine Arrow </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-09-2026, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T17:28:14-07:00","id":1562887,"title":"","content":"OK; I'm ready for comments. Two of the five got blocked, probably because I posted too quickly; but hopefully they'll be back. On my end:<br /> <br /> Yes, I know that Chthonos and Mythos have acquired unfortunate connotations, the first having come to mean \u201cof the underworld\u201d to many, and the second having come to be associated with H.P. Lovecraft's writing. I went with the names knowing this, in an attempt to reclaim their original meanings:<br /> <br /> Chthonos actually means \u201cof the Earth\u201d, and was originally used to refer to fertility gods and gods of the underworld, such as Persephone, her mother Demeter, and her husband Hades. Agriculture, both the growing and the harvesting, is every bit as chthonic as burial sites.<br /> <br /> The Greek word Mythos originally meant &quot;word,&quot; &quot;speech,&quot; &quot;tale,&quot; or &quot;story&quot;. Over time, it came to mean a traditional sacred story, a legend, or the structural plot of a dramatic work. It is in that sense, not the Lovecraftian sense, that I'm using it.<br /> <br /> Axios is being used as the name of a political publication currently. I'm using it in its original meaning, The Greek word axios translates to <b>&quot;</b>worthy,&quot; &quot;deserving,&quot; or &quot;suitable&quot;. Rooted in the concept of weighing scales, it originally described things of equal weight or matching value. Over time, it evolved to mean that a person's character, actions, or status balance out with what is right or deserved.<br /> <br /> The Greek word basileios means &quot;royal&quot;, &quot;kingly&quot;, or &quot;regal&quot;. It functions as an adjective derived from basileus, the Greek word for &quot;king&quot; or &quot;ruler&quot;.<br /> <br /> And finally, the Greek word teknos is actually spelled <b>techne</b>. It means art, craft, or skill. It describes the practical knowledge and the set rules used to make or do something. The term &quot;technos&quot; is not a standard standalone ancient Greek word, but rather a modern combining form or a grammatical variation derived from <i>techne</i>. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-08T20:02:01-07:00","id":1562889,"title":"","content":"So, I will say that there's quite a lot of overlap between the Teknos and the Obrimos in terms of &quot;grand design&quot; beliefs, even if one is slightly more flavored to religion than the other. I can't see the Cthonos just yet, so maybe they'll differ compared to the Thyrsus, but the other 3 at least do seem quite neat and unique!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26317-critian-caceorte","name":"Critian Caceorte","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T02:52:43-07:00","id":1562894,"title":"","content":"The Axios still read to me as very Scelesti/Seer coded. Debt default as attacking the fabric of the universe and legal agreements as unbreakable feels like the Lie. Like, both of those are not actually true. Debts and legal agreements can absolutely ruin people and they can feel like immovable elements of the cosmos, but they're ultimately not, they're social constructs that can be changed. It also feels odd that a spiritual path that sees the world in those terms, doesn't also have any concept of the forgiveness of debts. That would seem like the obvious way for the path to refute the Lie.<br /> <br /> I think Basileios is a cool name, and fits quite well. The description reads as very similar to the Obrimos, but that's maybe unavoidable.<br /> <br /> I like the Tecknos, but their realm and symbol feel a little random.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T07:32:10-07:00","id":1562897,"title":"","content":"I look at the Axios write up as defining that the universe works on balance. In physical science this is expressed as conservation laws. In society it is debt and binding legal agreements but also social obligations and bonds. A Seer might view things with a strict view; bureaucratic, uncaring, and focused on countable exchanges. A non-Seer might be more flexible looking at the balance of value but accepting that there are multiple stores of value that can be exchanged and values can be fluid based on situations and intention.<br /> <br /> Overall it feels very open to debates on fairness versus equity, the parable of the widow's offering (I'm sure their are other similar morality tales in other cultures), and various forms of organizing a society. It does make the scientific side of me wonder if magic is somehow connected to dark matter in that it clearly can violate normal conservation of energy; perhaps we simple aren't counting all the energy involved? A very Free Council thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T10:13:38-07:00","id":1562898,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madmarcus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1562880-the-other-five-paths?p=1562897#post1562897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In society it is debt and binding legal agreements but also social obligations and bonds. A Seer might view things with a strict view; bureaucratic, uncaring, and focused on countable exchanges. A non-Seer might be more flexible looking at the balance of value but accepting that there are multiple stores of value that can be exchanged and values can be fluid based on situations and intention.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a good way to go with it, but I don't see that in this write-up.<br /> <br /> That is, if it's even a problem. Like, a Path that inherently tends towards a Seer point of view is potentially pretty interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T11:14:13-07:00","id":1562899,"title":"","content":"That was not the intent. I have expanded the Axios write-up to more closely match the official Path write-ups, and hopefully also to address your concerns. Is this version better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T12:02:30-07:00","id":1562901,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1562880-the-other-five-paths?p=1562899#post1562899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have expanded the Axios write-up to more closely match the official Path write-ups, and hopefully also to address your concerns. Is this version better?</div> </div> </div> </div>Looks like it's vanished.<br /> <br /> I'm really liking the extended Basileios. They give me a really strong impression whilst the section on Prime being their inferior arcana gives them some needed distance from the Obrimos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T12:04:47-07:00","id":1562902,"title":"","content":"Aaand\u2026 it's blocked. Oops. (Hopefully, when a mod comes by and unlocks them, he'll post here to let me know.)<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I have revised every write-up that I still have access to. I changed the spelling from Teknos to Technos (apparently, the difference in spelling leads to wildly different meanings), and I shifted its focus to be a bit less obsessed with functionality and a bit <i>more </i>obsessed with aesthetics. <br /> <br /> Also: the quotes at the bottom of each write-up? They're there in part to help distinguish the new Path from the original Paths that have overlapping Ruling Arcana.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T12:09:07-07:00","id":1562903,"title":"","content":"Here's the relevant text that I added to the Axios to address your concerns:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\">However, independent arbiters understand that a ledger maintained solely through unyielding, punitive exactitude becomes an instrument of tyranny rather than justice. While the Seers of the Throne weaponize rigid debt without mercy to crush dissent, free Axios recognize that value is fundamentally fluid; trust, mercy, forgiveness, and future potential are valid stores of value that can be traded to clear a ledger before it breaks a life entirely. To forgive a debt is not to erase consequence, but to intentionally pivot the store of value from material or punitive ledger-balancing to social grace and strategic investment in a debtor's future.</div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T12:19:05-07:00","id":1562904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1562880-the-other-five-paths?p=1562901#post1562901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Looks like it's vanished.<br /> <br /> I'm really liking the extended Basileios. They give me a really strong impression whilst the section on Prime being their inferior arcana gives them some needed distance from the Obrimos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I was more concerned with them being too close to the Mastigos, given how confrontational both come across as.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T12:55:05-07:00","id":1562905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1562880-the-other-five-paths?p=1562904#post1562904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I was more concerned with them being too close to the Mastigos, given how confrontational both come across as.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think simply having different arcana does a lot of that job for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-09T19:37:03-07:00","id":1562914,"title":"","content":"Like the main structure, I'm seeing Basileios and Technos right now.<br /> <br /> For now it seems fitting, though I'm not sure if I agree with every choice of Inferior Arcana. But nothing big.<br /> <br /> Technos is particularly interesting to me since as is it restores the original intent of the roots for tech and art (its Latin &quot;equivalent&quot;).<br /> <br /> Art as a pure thought pursuit of appearance over function is a 17th century invention that works far more as gatekeeping of value for cultural production than the abstract intellect over base needs it's purported to mean.<br /> <br /> Historically art is everything you make through technique and skill you can master, and there is no result where function or beauty are absent as considerations. For this to happen it should be able to exist without form, from intent with no purpose.<br /> <br /> Similarly, Aesthetics is originally the philosophy of beauty, sure, but beauty was not defined by the Aesthetes as pleasing in form alone. For them the secret to understand beauty is that it is a sensation, not a property, and a sensation guided by everything the object means for us. It is goodness, function, memory, symbolism and so much more. Beauty for them was not what remains when evaluation is stripped of all other concerns, but rather their synthesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-10T17:34:36-07:00","id":1562993,"title":"","content":"Okay; everything's active, and I've expanded all write-ups so that they're now nearly as thorough as the official ones found in the core book; the main thing missing is quotes where each talks about the others. I'll be revising the initial post to provide overall context for them, such as how to use them in a chronicle. In the future, I plan to add material paralleling that found for the original Paths in <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> and <b>Nameless and Accursed</b>. <br /> <br /> So: thoughts? What works, what doesn't? I've already taken advice concerning the Axios and the Technos and incorporated it into the write-ups; I'm not opposed to taking constructive criticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T01:48:44-07:00","id":1563003,"title":"","content":"Love the Chthonos. I just think they're a really clear concept.<br /> <br /> The Axios having Life as inferior is quite inspired. I think it answers my criticism by incorporating it into the write-up.<br /> <br /> Also, adding a sentence or two to explain how the paths can come to terms with their inferior arcana is a good idea.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1562880-the-other-five-paths?p=1562993#post1562993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the future, I plan to add material paralleling that found for the original Paths in <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> and <b>Nameless and Accursed</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was meaning to ask if you were thinking of doing some Dur-Abzu. Like, whilst the 2e Paths are much improved from 1e, I personally found the contrast of the Ziggurats really clarified what the paths were about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T06:59:31-07:00","id":1563005,"title":"","content":"I like them. I'm not sure I have any particularly useful thoughts on specific ones but rereading the set did give me a couple of tangential impressions.<br /> <br /> Having more paths with different mixtures of primary arcana feels like it removes some of the mechanical push for legacies. I'm not sure how I feel about that. It might allow legacies to really shine because there is less push to find one that gives you the extra primary arcana that you really want to make your character fit your concept. Potentially it also allows a few characters to fit more neatly into a path instead of needing a path+legacy to really capture their mindset.<br /> <br /> Related to that last point I do have a slight role playing issue with adding new paths. The more paths there are the more it feels like the path = mindset noose gets tighter. In practice at the table this probably isn't a big deal but as I read your descriptions they feel even more prescriptive of the personality and mindset of each path than the my memory of the official path descriptions. For example your Basileios is all about command and rigid authority. Yet my instant connection when I think Forces + Spirit is a Taoist mage who has authority over natural forces and spirits but does not show it in the rigid, commanding way that you describe. The earlier comments about Axios and the different views of myself and Michael are similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28478-madmarcus","name":"Madmarcus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T08:43:59-07:00","id":1563008,"title":"","content":"I wasn't intending on them coming across quite so bossy. I'll see about revising the text to tone that down. Yes, they command spirits; that's what differentiates them from shamans, who negotiate with spirits. But just because you have the authority, that doesn't mean that you should, or will, abuse it. That's more of a Seeds of the Throne thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T10:46:00-07:00","id":1563012,"title":"","content":"I would want a write up on how things develop when the Mage doesn't quite buy in the Watchtower perspective too much, but that's for another moment.<br /> <br /> For now I'll give ideas one at a time, starting with current Axios:<br /> <br /> My current impression is that commerce and contract is a narrower concept than it needs to be, and maybe taking a step back will be useful to clean and refine.<br /> <br /> While money, credit and contracts operationalize our systems of exchange, the underlying cultural basin where the notion of fair traid arises is the concept of Reciprocity, a pillar of many social, but also spiritual and magical practices.<br /> <br /> Ubuntu has been a quite popular formalization of this notion recently, but it used to be quite a common idea, especially before the separation of Nature and Artificial in Modern Europe's philosophy.<br /> <br /> The world exists as a web of relationships. All things within are defined not by an immanent nature, but by their relationships with all else. It is not a human property to owe and be owed, but the condition of existence itself. There is no &quot;I&quot; that exists alone.<br /> <br /> And it is in this Web of All Things that we exist where our actions occur, always affecting other things. Every definition is a relationship, every existence is an actor and every action is itself an exchange.<br /> <br /> Reciprocity becomes the First Natural Law: do for others so they do for your. Fulfill your part as it's your obligation, and share the benefits of others doing theirs. Be grateful for what you're given, demand what you're owed, return to the world in proper fashion and recognize your role as a fellow being. Reciprocate with everything, for everything is a part of this system, animals, rocks, weather. Reap the benefits of repaying your debts and the consequences for failing to do so, as they'll come in due time.<br /> <br /> One of the benefits of this thought system is that it's animistic without need for ontological spirits: you don't thank the god of the mountain or the spirit of the mountain, but the mountain itself, and that's enough, because the relations are real without need for a conscious mind and by the law of nature rather than deliberation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T15:43:17-07:00","id":1563022,"title":"","content":"I have rewritten the Basileios as outlined above, and I'm in the process of rewriting the Axios to take your observations into account. They'll probably cease to be the Axios, as the Path name is generally a Greek translation of the Path's quality; so changing that quality from Value to Reciprocity will require a rethinking of the Path name as well. <br /> <br /> If does means that the Paths probably won't be in alphabetical order anymore; but c'est la vie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-11T16:49:29-07:00","id":1563023,"title":"","content":"\u2026and the new Xenios are awaiting moderator approval. Le *sigh*\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-13T16:09:22-07:00","id":1563073,"title":"","content":"Okay. The Xenios, formerly Axios, are live.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T13:10:00-07:00","id":1563231,"title":"","content":"I would like to offer an entirely vibes-based critique of the choice of tarot symbolism.<br /> <br /> Xenios: The Magician and Judgement are perfect. However, I think there are other evocative elements to draw out. The Magician card is sometimes a juggler (I believe the card was originally meant to be like, a magician who does tricks, not a wizard.) which has symbolism around trickery and charlatanry which is potentially very appropriate for a trader path. Meanwhile Judgement, even in the Awakening version of the tarot has the symbolism of the Christian last judgement, with its final settling of all debts. Also, given the alterations to the Path, Justice might also be appropriate?<br /> <br /> Basileios: The Chariot is great, no issues there. However, I think the Hierophant is the Obrimos' card. Like, sacred doctrine feels to me like an attribute of Prime rather than Spirit or Forces (it's also the Prelacy of the Exarch of Prime). I would instead suggest the Emperor. Like, to me the archetype of the path seems to be that of a mystical autocrat (also, not speaking Greek, Basileios can only bring up images of the Byzantine Emperors).<br /> <br /> Chthonos: This is tricky. I get the duality idea that's going on... But I still think it needs to have the Wheel of Fortune. I don't know what you do with the other card, probably just leave the Hermit?<br /> <br /> Mythos: Wheel of Fortune and High Priestess are fine.<br /> <br /> Teknos: I think the World is a good choice. The Tower really isn't. Like, the Tower is being blown apart and the occupants falling to the ground. It's not ambiguous enough that an unorthodox reading works for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-18T15:11:12-07:00","id":1563235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1562880-the-other-five-paths?p=1563231#post1563231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to offer an entirely vibes-based critique of the choice of tarot symbolism.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd like to chime in, though a bit less vibes and more practitioner.<br /> <br /> Judgment I think fits perfectly despite the reference being Christian Eschatology. This is what using the regular Tarot entails, better to use another set of cards than leave Judgment out of the Ultimate Ledger.<br /> <br /> And I'd avoid Justice here just because it would overlap, so I'll focus on what to do with Magician. It's not about charlatanism, though, that's a modern reading. The old Juggler card was an alternative to the Fool.<br /> <br /> The Magician in the old times was a scientist, a natural philosopher with a penchant for practical experiments and exploration. It's a card of action and the directed impetus to start something (not necessarily the means to reach the end). I find it somewhat weird here, though not completely out of place, but it's not a card of materiality, just action.<br /> <br /> What about the Devil? While the first reading is obvious, it's actually the card of material things and earthly desires regardless of morals, not only for lack of morals. It is the card of embodiment, of material possessions and their trade, it's food, coin, sex and the physical, material reality that's here with or without more elaborated meanings.<br /> <br /> For the Basileios I fully agree and go further. The Hierophant is less a leader and more a stern teacher. It doesn't command, it judge and chastise. It's holier-than-thou and seeks social conformity to tradition, not normal hierarchy.<br /> <br /> Emperor is stewardship and leadership. It takes in its hands the responsibility to direct and get things done. It may lead by example or impose with command, but it is taking decision and furthering goals. The Hierophant tells you why you should follow proper hierarchy. The Emperor sits at the top with or without their approval, as someone has to do.<br /> <br /> For the Cthonos, the Wheel of Fortune is more random chance than cycles. But I wouldn't use the Hermit or Sun, either. Rather I'd start with the Empress. It's the card of nurturing and protection, of authority as a form of care, that of a parent rather than boss (although it can be a caring boss, the archetypal military leader that has the well being of the unit against outside threats as priority is not an Emperor, but an Empress).<br /> <br /> While the card of natural cycles is actually Death, the card that cares for nature and loves it is generally the Empress, and she accepts her charges as they are and by their nature, not her whims.<br /> <br /> For seconds there are options. Death is cycles, and in fact maybe too perfect, there's a reason why in the card the pale rider acts as a harvester, not an executioner. Justice is balance and the active care to ensure it rather than post-hoc dishing final consequence. Temperance is avoidance of extremes and integration of contradictions, take what you need, give what you must, without greed or sacrifice.<br /> <br /> Mythos I only want to remind that Bard vs Sage isn't actually a duality, but the original concept of a Bard, not only in Celtic culture but the archetypal role as seen in countless other societies. Where collective memory lives in oral tradition more than written text, the Aedos is not an improviser, but a record keeper, and inspiration isn't about novel ideas, but gospel truth. But on tarot, yeah, Fortune and Priestess all the way.<br /> <br /> Technos I want first to say that I'd avoid using The World or The Fool on principle. The World is not just physical realization, it's integration of all that came, in all areas, all Arcana at once. And you got it, the Tower is destruction, it's end in a shocking fashion. Cataclysm and ruination, it's not about the tower built but how it crumbles under absolute destructive power.<br /> <br /> Instead I'd use the Magician here, and the Sun too. The first is the card of those who seek to make things happen, to bring possibility into existence. A maker, an artist, an explorer, it takes the road to make its will into reality. For the other side I'm between the foggy, dreamlike inspiration of the Moon and the positive realization of the Sun. If the Devil isn't used elsewhere, it may also fit here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-19T08:52:51-07:00","id":1563248,"title":"","content":"Yeah; be careful when advising to not just look at a given Path in isolation. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> already seems to be aware of this, but these need to be viewed as a set, and also as a subset of a \u201cTen Paths\u201d system (including the five official Paths). And within these sets, each Tarot card needs to be used no more than once.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-20T12:58:09-07:00","id":1563289,"title":"","content":"I like the Sun for the Cthonos as it can stand for illuminating what is hidden (the Cthonos going into the Underworld and &quot;fixing&quot; things) and the conscious mind (engagement in the physical world). It plays as a nice opposition to the Thyrsus Moon, the unconscious/spirit world. The Empress fits the Cthonos very well as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> explains above and sits as a good mirror again to the Thyrsus Hermit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Lead Writer for the Savage Age of Werewolf: the Apocalypse: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/428750/Ghost-Lineages-The-Advanced-Players-Guide-to-the-Savage-Age\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Lineages</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/312700/The-Rise-of-the-Garou-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Two\" target=\"_blank\">Rise of the Garou</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/331302/Tools-of-Extinction-The-Savage-Age-Volume-Three\" target=\"_blank\">Tools of Extinction</a>, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/352717/Tribebook-Wlewa\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook: Wlewa</a>.<br /> <br /> Want RPGs in libraries? Check out my book, <a href=\"http://www.abc-clio.com/ABC-CLIOCorporate/product.aspx?pc=A3951P\" target=\"_blank\">Dragons in the Stacks</a>. Now with <a href=\"http://www.ennie-awards.com/blog/2015-ennie-award-nominees-and-spotlight-winners/\" target=\"_blank\">awards</a>!<br /> \u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1813-grimjaws","name":"grimjaws","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1813_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}